  "body": "## What changed\n\nBore clears wide holes with concentric rings at each cut level.\nEach radial sweep opens the next ring band.\nThe final ring finishes the wall.\nDetect holes now keeps these wide holes.\n\nThe radial step is at most 0.8 times the cutter reach at the floor.\nSmall holes keep their previous single-ring path when its floor bands meet.\nThe plan refuses more than 4,096 rings before allocation.\nIt also refuses an unresolved floor band, including a ball cutter at a blind flat floor.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe previous path cut one radial sweep and one wall ring.\nThe width guard refused holes where these cuts left an interior core.\nThe blind bull-nose estimate also used the full tool radius and could leave an interior floor ridge.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe first pin failed on unchanged code at a 20 mm hole with a 6 mm tool.\nThe restored code passes seven motion pins and five app integration tests.\n\n- `wide_bore_rings_clear_the_whole_floor` covers three wide ratios, both directions, blind holes, through holes, and wall allowance.\n- `wide_bull_nose_bores_clear_the_floor_without_an_interior_ridge` checks the flat floor inside the wall fillet.\n- `ball_bore_needs_positive_floor_reach_and_corner_must_fit` checks ball reach and named refusals.\n- `bore_ring_count_enforces_its_allocation_budget` checks the allocation boundary and non-finite radius.\n- `bore_ring_budget_refuses_extreme_holes_by_name` checks the visible budget refusal.\n- App tests cover detection, manual hole entry, generation, verification, and project reopening.\n\nAll three mutations failed and passed after restoration:\n\n- Copying the upstream generator back left a 0.480 mm floor gap.\n- Removing the ring budget allowed 4,097 rings.\n- Restoring the full-radius blind estimate left a 1.966 mm floor ridge.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed with zero failed steps.\nThe mapped motion and app suites took 16.9 minutes.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The NC and CL golden diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine cut or release gate ran.\nThe app fixture uses 0.1 mm wall allowance because its 64-facet STL wall lies inside the nominal circle.\nVerification rejected the zero-allowance path on that faceted fixture.\nThe motion coverage pins include zero allowance.\nThe cutter corner still leaves the intended fillet at the wall.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone found in the expected files before the claim.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: Bore clears wide holes with bounded concentric rings and clears blind bull-nose interior floor ridges.\n\nFixes #1566\n",
